# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include application source packages that the broad build-artifact patterns
# above (lib/, models/) would otherwise swallow. These are first-party source,
# not build output or ML artifacts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Keep this list complete. backend/ml/models/ was missed when the first two
# were added, so backend/ml/ stayed unimportable -- its __init__ imports
# backend.ml.models, which had never been committed. Nothing imports
# backend.ml, so no test caught it.
#
# To check for others:
#   git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard --directory
#
!frontend/src/lib/
!frontend/src/lib/**
!backend/app/models/
!backend/app/models/**
!backend/ml/models/
!backend/ml/models/**

# A `!dir/**` re-include also un-ignores build output underneath it, so put the
# artifact patterns back for these subtrees specifically.
backend/app/models/**/__pycache__/
backend/ml/models/**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
